			"notes": "# Steve AI 1.8.0 — Local-first autonomy\n\nSteve can now plan and execute supported resource gathering, crafting, and smelting goals locally, using the language model only when local planning cannot handle the request.\n\n## Added\n\n- Local planning for simple `craft` / `make`, `smelt`, and `gather` / `collect` / `mine` goals.\n- Support for registered item IDs, mod namespaces, and simple English item names.\n- Inventory-aware planning: request a desired inventory total and Steve produces only the missing quantity. Already satisfied goals complete without consuming materials.\n- Offline operation for supported goals with `[autonomy] maxLlmCallsPerGoal = 0`.\n- The `localPlanning` configuration option, enabled by default.\n- Seven dedicated Minecraft GameTests covering crafting, gathering, furnace smelting, existing inventory, pause/stop, denied permissions, and unsupported offline requests.\n\n## Fixed\n\n- Local execution no longer depends on initializing a language model or having an available LLM call budget.\n- Prerequisite planning preserves requested quantities and accounts for ingredients already in inventory.\n- Prerequisite nesting is limited to eight levels to prevent unbounded dependency chains.\n- Local planning outcomes use valid execution state transitions.\n\n## Behavior and compatibility\n\n- Existing permissions, pause/stop controls, bounded recovery, and deterministic goal verification remain enforced.\n- Compound or unknown requests still use LLM fallback. With a zero-call budget, unsupported requests stop with an explanation.\n- This release provides bounded local task planning; it does not add unrestricted offline language understanding or new proactive behavior.\n- **Minecraft:** 1.20.1\n- **Loader:** Forge (built against 47.2.0)\n- **Java:** 17 or newer\n\n## Installation\n\nDownload `steve-ai-mod-1.8.0.jar` from the release assets and place it in your Forge installation's `mods` directory. Replace the previous Steve AI JAR instead of keeping both versions. The installable JAR includes its required runtime libraries; do not use a `-slim.jar` build.\n\nThe accompanying `.sha256` file can be used to verify the download.\n\n## Offline examples\n\n```text\ncraft 8 oak_planks\nsmelt 16 iron_ingots\ngather 4 oak_log\n```\n\nQuantities are inventory targets, not additional amounts. Recipe output batches may exceed the missing count.\n\nImplemented in [PR #5](https://github.com/gnustella-lab/Steve-AI/pull/5)."
		}
